    "https://www.kenyon.edu/careers-outcomes/career-development-office/for-employers/": {
      "title": "Calls to ActionNavigation",
      "description": "For Employers | Kenyon College Skip to main content Kenyon College Home Calls to Action Navigation Apply Visit Menu You are here: Home Careers & Outcomes Career Development Office For Employers Employers Hire curiosity, discipline, empathy, passion — hire Kenyon. Explore This Section Close Explore This Section Mentorship Internships and Research Career and Graduate Program Advising For Employers Only at Kenyon Contact Us Hiring Good People Has Never Been Easier We are here to make recruiting simple. We will work with you directly to ensure your recruitment needs get to the right people on campus — and ultimately to the right student and alumni talent! Recruit with Handshake Create an employer profile then share events, jobs and internships directly to Kenyon. Let us know when you connect and we'll give your opportunities added promotion! Questions? Handshake offers support but we're happy to help, too. Join or Log In to Handshake Handshake Support for Employers Your Applicant Pool Awaits Want to start recruiting now, at this very moment? We have talented students who are open to outreach from our employers seeking new talent. Use Kenyon Candidates to find a candidate and invite them to apply. View Kenyon Candidates Hire Kenyon You know the quality of Kenyon students and are ready to advocate for them within your company. Use this form to tell us how you can help a student get noticed at your company. Fill out the \"Hire Kenyon\" Form Want to be a Mentor? Alumni and families interested in mentoring students can review career development volunteering options. See Volunteer Opportunities Become an Employer Partner Take your campus visibility to the next level by becoming an employer partner. We'll work with you to create an effective campus strategy that will increase exposure to our highly talented and diverse students. Additional partnership opportunities include: Provide raffle prizes (and receive campus-wide brand awareness) in our award-winning Rewards Program Reserve dedicated space on campus to interview students (virtual options, too) Set up an informational table in Kenyon’s singular Dining Hall, gaining brand visibility from all students Create simulated exercises to immediately see prospective talented students Or volunteer an idea of your own... Contact Kenyon's director of employer relations to begin a conversation. Joshua Lisko Director of Employer Relations Contact P hone Number 740-427-5217 E mail Address lisko1@kenyon.edu Location Chalmers Library, 255 Alicia Misarti Director of Internships Contact P hone Number 740-427-5011 E mail Address misartia@kenyon.edu Location Chalmers 254 Kenyon Address Gambier , Ohio 43022 , USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Navigation Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn tiktok Visiting Kenyon Navigation Directions Campus Map Kenyon Commits To Navigation Mission & Values Accessibility Non-Discrimination Privacy Kenyon Affiliates Brown Family Environmental Center The Gund Kenyon Review Philander Chase Conservancy Footer Navigation Employment Bookstore Emergency Title IX Policies Make a Gift © Copyright 2026 Site Menu Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Search Submit CTAs Navigation Apply Visit Site Navigation Academics Departments and Majors Our Faculty Advising & Resources Experiential Learning Global Learning Student Research Writing at Kenyon Library Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Visit Kenyon Apply to Kenyon Financial Aid & Scholarships Connect with Us Request Information Campus Life Inclusion & Belonging Residential Life Dining on Campus Health & Safety Civic Engagement Sustainability & Green Initiatives Clubs & Organizations Arts & Culture Careers & Outcomes Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Athletics Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Explore Kenyon Navigation in brief in pictures in numbers in our own words in the world on a tour Links For Navigation Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community New Students Close"
    },
    "https://www.kenyon.edu/academics/our-faculty/": {
      "title": "Calls to ActionNavigation",
      "description": "Our Faculty | Kenyon College Skip to main content Kenyon College Home Calls to Action Navigation Apply Visit Menu You are here: Home Academics Our Faculty Our Faculty Students and faculty are partners in inquiry. Explore This Section Close Explore This Section Departments and Majors Our Faculty Advising & Resources Experiential Learning Global Learning Student Research Writing at Kenyon Library Academic Calendar One phenomenal teacher can change your life. Kenyon is home to more than 200 engaged and dedicated professors who devote their full attention to their students — even long after graduation. Kenyon faculty go above and beyond to be more than just partners in learning and inquiry — they make the time to genuinely know you, to help shape your future. Universe Explorer Associate Professor of Physics Madeline Wade , winner of a prestigious NSF CAREER grant, helps the LIGO Scientific Collaboration unlock the mysteries of spacetime. Creative Expressionist “I think writers are obsessive creatures,” says Ira Sukrungruang , the professor of creative writing who channels his obsessions into invigorating the literary life of Kenyon. Economic Experimenter How much is social media really worth? To find out, economist Jay Corrigan ponied up and paid Kenyon students real money to give up their Facebook accounts. Justice Seeker Political scientist Jackie McAllister doesn’t quite hunt down war criminals, but she does study how international tribunals can reduce violence and promote peace. Feature Filmmaker Jon Tazewell ’84 directed the first full-length film produced by Kenyon’s film department, the timely and stirring college-set drama “Gotta Get Down To It.” Legal Advocate With research poised at the intersection of race, children, psychology and the law, Margaret Stevenson works to improve the justice system for marginalized groups. Neanderthal Defender Anthropologist Bruce Hardy is a friend to our much maligned ancient relatives. His cutting-edge research proves they were more than dull, hairy, stooped savages. AI Wizard Could self-driving cars decide which lives to save in an accident? Does social media make people angry on purpose? Kate Elkins explores the clash of tech and humanity. Thought leaders, inspired minds Kenyon faculty members are authors, artists and researchers immersed in scholarly and creative projects. 200+ faculty across 50 majors, minors and concentrations 100% of full-time faculty hold a Ph.D. or other terminal degree in their field 100% of courses are taught by professors 9:1 student-to-faculty ratio 60-Second Syllabus: Faculty Favorites From dance, film and literature to science and international relations, Kenyon professors give brief overviews of some of their favorite courses. Watch the Trailer View the Full Playlist Faculty News Faculty Field Notes Several faculty members who spent the summer months abroad learning, teaching and researching wrote virtual postcards to the campus community. New Faculty Bring New Insight Four tenure-track faculty join the College for the 2026-27 academic year. Dianna Shandy Appointed as Kenyon’s Next Provost A seasoned academic leader who has served both Macalester and Augustana colleges, Shandy will join Kenyon as its chief academic officer beginning Aug. 1. Four Faculty Named to Endowed Positions Faculty members from across the College were appointed to endowed professorships that support their work effective July 1. Kenyon Address Gambier , Ohio 43022 , USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Navigation Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn tiktok Visiting Kenyon Navigation Directions Campus Map Kenyon Commits To Navigation Mission & Values Accessibility Non-Discrimination Privacy Kenyon Affiliates Brown Family Environmental Center The Gund Kenyon Review Philander Chase Conservancy Footer Navigation Employment Bookstore Emergency Title IX Policies Make a Gift © Copyright 2026 Site Menu Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Search Submit CTAs Navigation Apply Visit Site Navigation Academics Departments and Majors Our Faculty Advising & Resources Experiential Learning Global Learning Student Research Writing at Kenyon Library Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Visit Kenyon Apply to Kenyon Financial Aid & Scholarships Connect with Us Request Information Campus Life Inclusion & Belonging Residential Life Dining on Campus Health & Safety Civic Engagement Sustainability & Green Initiatives Clubs & Organizations Arts & Culture Careers & Outcomes Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Athletics Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Explore Kenyon Navigation in brief in pictures in numbers in our own words in the world on a tour Links For Navigation Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community New Students Close"
    },
    "https://www.kenyon.edu/careers-outcomes/": {
      "title": "Calls to ActionNavigation",
      "description": "Careers & Outcomes | Kenyon College Skip to main content Kenyon College Home Calls to Action Navigation Apply Visit Menu Careers & Outcomes Kenyon grads do more than land jobs. They launch meaningful careers. Explore This Section Close Explore This Section Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Your future starts now. Where will you be in five, 10 or even 20 years? From your very first day, Kenyon faculty, staff and an expansive alumni network are here to help you explore and shape your career path with rewarding experiences inside and outside of the classroom. The results are pretty inspiring. 90% of 2025 graduates were employed, continuing their education or committed to other plans within six months. Learn how Kenyon grads launch meaningful careers . Fulbright Force Year in and year out, Kenyon is a top bachelor institution for producing Fulbright Fellows. Learn more about Fulbrights . 93% of Kenyon students who apply to graduate school attend one of their top three choices. Futures in Medicine Year after year, Kenyon applicants to medical school are accepted at double the national average. Learn more about pre-med at Kenyon . What can you do with a Kenyon degree? Anything that matters to you. Whether jumping straight into a career or pursuing further study, you’ll be well positioned for the first of many next steps in the industry you aim to influence. Here’s a snapshot of where the Class of 2025 landed. Explore alumni careers by major Expert Guidance, Rewarding Opportunities From internships and job shadows to fieldwork and research, your team of career and faculty advisors provides you with the resources and expertise to explore and pursue a meaningful career. Get an internship, anywhere. At Kenyon, you can gain rewarding experience from internships on campus or in the local community, or pursue opportunities further afield over the summer. Internships Career Development Office Dig into research. Through our flagship summer research programs and year-long projects, you can collaborate with faculty on questions as big as the universe. Student Research Secure a fellowship. If exploring the world is your goal, you’ll get expert advice from faculty and staff who have helped a record number of students win prestigious fellowships and scholarships. Fellowships & Awards Find a mentor, or several. A career is more than a job. Kenyon’s team of career advisors and expansive alumni network can help you marry passion and skill to forge a meaningful future. Career Development Office The Kenyon Network Our network is your team. With access to hundreds of alumni and parent career mentors, you’ll start your journey with a leg up. Connect with accomplished Kenyon alumni from around the world for job shadowing, resume reviews, internships, interview prep and more. Setting the Scene Through a job shadow with set decorator Rosemary Brandenburg ’78, a film major experienced the ins and outs of a professional production. Categories Alumni Careers Open Mind in Year One - related video Running time: 2:18 Open Mind in Year One First Person: Student Life at Kenyon In his first year, Hyun Cho '26 explored course topics and career interests with an open mind. Categories Careers Athletics Alumni Finding Her Audience In the News Alumni connections helped Mia Sherin ’22 broaden her horizons as a writer, leading to a budding career in New York City. Categories Alumni Careers Let the Sunshine In Kenyon News Environmental studies major Jayne Gelman ’22 is drawn toward the light of a career in solar energy development. Categories Science Student Life You might recognize our alumni. Kenyon graduates are in good company. From the U. S. Ambassador to Ukraine, Bridget Brink ’91, to legendary philanthropist and actor Paul Newman ’49, generations of Kenyon alumni have put their talents to work across the globe and professional fields. It’s a legacy that both impresses and inspires. More notable alumni . Bookshelf Titans Kenyon authors like John Green ’00 make repeat appearances on The New York Times best-seller lists with mainstays like “The Fault In Our Stars,” “Sweetbitter,” “Seabiscuit” and “Ragtime.” Best in Class From Oscars to Pulitzers, Kenyon alumni earn top honors in their industries. Allison Janney ’82 is one of the most accomplished actors in Hollywood. Thought Provokers Kenyon alumni help shape the national dialogue. “Pod Save America,” co-hosted by Tommy Vietor ’02, is one of the country’s most downloaded and influential podcasts. Change Agents In and out of the halls of power, Kenyon alumni are voices for change. The Obama Foundation recognized lawyer Colette Pichon Battle ’97 for her work to protect Gulf Coast communities affected by climate change. Kenyon Address Gambier , Ohio 43022 , USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Navigation Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn tiktok Visiting Kenyon Navigation Directions Campus Map Kenyon Commits To Navigation Mission & Values Accessibility Non-Discrimination Privacy Kenyon Affiliates Brown Family Environmental Center The Gund Kenyon Review Philander Chase Conservancy Footer Navigation Employment Bookstore Emergency Title IX Policies Make a Gift © Copyright 2026 Site Menu Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Search Submit CTAs Navigation Apply Visit Site Navigation Academics Departments and Majors Our Faculty Advising & Resources Experiential Learning Global Learning Student Research Writing at Kenyon Library Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Visit Kenyon Apply to Kenyon Financial Aid & Scholarships Connect with Us Request Information Campus Life Inclusion & Belonging Residential Life Dining on Campus Health & Safety Civic Engagement Sustainability & Green Initiatives Clubs & Organizations Arts & Culture Careers & Outcomes Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Athletics Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Explore Kenyon Navigation in brief in pictures in numbers in our own words in the world on a tour Links For Navigation Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community New Students Close"
