    "https://www.kenyon.edu/careers-outcomes/career-development-office/": {
      "title": "Calls to ActionNavigation",
      "description": "Career Development Office | Kenyon College Skip to main content Kenyon College Home Calls to Action Navigation Apply Visit Menu You are here: Home Careers & Outcomes Career Development Office The Career Development Office Your success is our priority. Explore This Section Close Explore This Section Mentorship Internships and Research Career and Graduate Program Advising For Employers Only at Kenyon Contact Us Success takes hard work. But if you're at Kenyon, you're prepared for it. Here you have teams of people to support you: faculty, alumni, peers, and staff that together create a vast network of talented individuals who will help you succeed, and will celebrate your every accomplishment along the way! Advising for Career and Graduate School Our advisors and extensive network of alumni and parents can help you clarify goals and explore career paths. And they are here for you after graduation, as well. Advising and Programs Health Professions Advising Internships and Research Opportunities Know the value of your skills by applying them in new contexts. Internships and research opportunities at Kenyon and beyond help you to do just that. Internships and Research at Kenyon Past Interns Mentorship Relationships aren't just good for your soul, they're good for your career too. Our alumni are some of the easiest people to talk to, and they can mentor you to success. Mentorship at Kenyon Only at Kenyon Experimentation isn't reserved for Kenyon labs. We routinely pilot new career programs at Kenyon that make a splash in higher education. Only at Kenyon After Kenyon Our alumni become change-makers. Learn more about our alumni outcomes and students' first destinations. After Kenyon Class of 2025 Outcomes Volunteer Opportunities Alumni play a critical role in students’ professional development through mentorship, hiring referrals and sharing industry expertise. Learn More Fast-Paced Summers From working in the legal field to digital marketing, Kenyon students land meaningful internships each summer. Here's a recent sampling. D.C. Explorer Luna Hicks ’26 explored her political science major in greater depth during a summer in Washington, D.C., through an internship at the National Security Institute and professional development experiences at the Ronald Reagan Institute Academy for Civics Education and Democracy. Coral Reef Researcher Environmental studies major Arianna Flota ’27 put her lifelong passion for protecting coral reefs to work as a researcher at the Mote Marine Laboratory in the Summerland Key, Florida. Aspiring Attorney Sacha Franjola ‘26 found unexpected connections between art history studies and law in an internship with the United States Attorney’s Office for the Southern District of New York’s National Security and International Narcotics unit. Legal Advocate As an investigative intern for the Legal Aid Society of New York , sociology major Julián Clivillés ’25 (second row, center) assisted attorneys by gathering facts and interviewing witnesses. Newsworthy Highlights Kenyon’s Exclusive Internship Programs Kenyon News Professional development opportunities offered exclusively to Kenyon students provide the perfect path to future career success. Categories Careers Kenyon Tops Med-School Acceptance Rate Kenyon News Kenyon students pursuing professions in medicine and healthcare are served by a multitude of experiential learning opportunities. Categories Careers Career Development Program Receives National Acclaim Kenyon News The Career Development Office received a prestigious award for its program that encourages students to take advantage of its resources by offering exclusive prizes and perks. Categories Careers Fulbright Success Continues Kenyon News Eight recent graduates have received Fulbright fellowships, the U.S. Department of State’s  flagship international academic exchange program. Categories Kenyon in the World Career Development Office Contact P hone Number 740-427-5165 E mail Address cdo@kenyon.edu Location Chalmers Library 259 (second floor) 103 College Drive Gambier, Ohio 43022 Connect Twitter LinkedIn Instagram Kenyon Address Gambier , Ohio 43022 , USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Navigation Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn tiktok Visiting Kenyon Navigation Directions Campus Map Kenyon Commits To Navigation Mission & Values Accessibility Non-Discrimination Privacy Kenyon Affiliates Brown Family Environmental Center The Gund Kenyon Review Philander Chase Conservancy Footer Navigation Employment Bookstore Emergency Title IX Policies Make a Gift © Copyright 2026 Site Menu Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Search Submit CTAs Navigation Apply Visit Site Navigation Academics Departments and Majors Our Faculty Advising & Resources Experiential Learning Global Learning Student Research Writing at Kenyon Library Academic Calendar Admissions & Aid Visit Kenyon Apply to Kenyon Financial Aid & Scholarships Connect with Us Request Information Campus Life Inclusion & Belonging Residential Life Dining on Campus Health & Safety Civic Engagement Sustainability & Green Initiatives Clubs & Organizations Arts & Culture Careers & Outcomes Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Athletics Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Explore Kenyon Navigation in brief in pictures in numbers in our own words in the world on a tour Links For Navigation Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Community New Students Close"
