    "https://www.kenyon.edu/careers-outcomes/the-kenyon-network/": {
      "title": "Calls to ActionNavigation",
      "description": "The Kenyon Network | Kenyon College Skip to main content Kenyon College Home Calls to Action Navigation Apply Visit Menu You are here: Home Careers & Outcomes The Kenyon Network The Kenyon Network A global community of Kenyon mentors will help shape your perspective and future. Explore This Section Close Explore This Section Career Development Office Internships Fellowships & Awards After Kenyon The Kenyon Network Outcomes Report 2025 Mentorship Matters When you join the Kenyon community, you join a global network of alumni and parent career mentors from more than 200 industries who are eager to get to know you and help connect you with job shadows, resume reviews, internships and interviews. Tap into the Kenyon Network This global network of Kenyon alumni and parent career mentors can offer invaluable insight and support. Complete a job shadow A job shadow is an opportunity for students to explore a career of interest by observing an alumnus, alumna, parent or other volunteer in their place of work, typically for a period of 1-5 days. Try an externship Externships are project-based learning opportunities designed and offered by Kenyon alumni and parents who offer coaching and feedback. Join the Kenyon Network on LinkedIn to connect with professionals in your field of interest. Kenyon Network on LinkedIn The Kenyon Network at Work Setting the Scene Through a job shadow with set decorator Rosemary Brandenburg ’78, a film major experienced the ins and outs of a professional production. Categories Alumni Careers Open Mind in Year One - related video Running time: 2:18 Open Mind in Year One First Person: Student Life at Kenyon In his first year, Hyun Cho '26 explored course topics and career interests with an open mind. Categories Careers Athletics Alumni Finding Her Audience In the News Alumni connections helped Mia Sherin ’22 broaden her horizons as a writer, leading to a budding career in New York City. Categories Alumni Careers Let the Sunshine In Kenyon News Environmental studies major Jayne Gelman ’22 is drawn toward the light of a career in solar energy development. Categories Science Student Life Kenyon alumni believe in giving back. What better way than by sharing their professional passions and know-how? Physics major Christian Solorio ’18 shadows Megan Harvey ’05, a flight controller for the International Space Station. India Amos ’17 shadows James Fleming '91 and Anna Bammerlin ’14 at the U.S. Agency for International Development. John Hays ’82 gives Kristin Toms ’20 and Brady Furlich ’19 an insider’s look at Christie’s, the famous British auction house. Leticia Osei-Bonsu ’17 gets a taste of the food industry with Jeni’s Splendid Ice Creams brand ambassador Elizabeth McLees ’12. A double major in neuroscience and chemistry, Juliette Lowe '25 shadowed Dr. Ashley Karpinos '03, an associate professor at Vanderbilt University Medical Center who specializes in internal medicine and pediatrics sports medicine. Sascha Shapiro ’25 explored what a career in finance might look like when he met with Mac Carroll ’11 at GM Asset Management in New York City as part of a job shadow program organized by the Career Development Office. Kenyon students and alumni connect at a networking event. English and anthropology major Taylor Hazan ’19 shadows Susie Heimbach ’98 at the New York Public Library. Kenyon Address Gambier , Ohio 43022 , USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Navigation Instagram Facebook YouTube LinkedIn tiktok Visiting Kenyon Navigation Directions Campus Map Kenyon Commits To Navigation Mission & Values Accessibility Non-Discrimination Privacy Kenyon Affiliates Brown Family Environmental Center The Gund Kenyon Review Philander Chase Conservancy Footer Navigation Employment Bookstore Emergency Title IX Policies Make a Gift © Copyright 2026 Site Menu Secondary Navigation Apply Give News Events Directory Offices & Services Search Submit CTAs Navigation Apply Visit Site Navigation Academics Departments and Maj