    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/senior-associate-director-of-alumni-career-connections-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections",
      "description": "Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Back to Kenyon College Website My Profile Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections 493367 Gambier, OH, Ohio Alumni and Parent Engagement Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections. The Senior Associate Director of Alumni Career Connections co-reports to the Director of Alumni Engagement and the Dean of the Career Development Office (CDO). This role will direct the mentorship and alumni connections unit within the CDO and be responsible for executing the overall volunteerism and mentorship strategy related to careers and experiential education. Essential Functions Coordinate all Kenyon alumni career-related volunteer activities in conjunction with the Office of Alumni Engagement and Career Development Office. Oversee the Expert in Residence Program. Maintain accurate records in the SLATE Advancement database. Help coordinate alumni involvement with the “Kenyon City” programs associated with the Kenyon Keys. Recruit hosts for the job shadow and externship programs in conjunction with the Career Development Office. Collaborate with the Director of Employer Relations in the CDO to plan and execute career treks during Kenyon academic breaks to popular destinations among students. Connect students 1:1 with alumni mentors, establishing clear expectations and structure for successful mentoring relationships. Work with the Experiential Learning (EL) committee to embed job shadow and externships in the tracking and reflection mechanisms of the ELR. Manage the administration of the “Just Ask” Distribute the annual Kenyon Candidates resume books to alumni in conjunction with Advancement Communications Work closely with the Director of Employer Partnerships and Director of Internships to create a unified communication strategy to alumni, parents, and employers regarding career engagement opportunities. Coordinate on-campus skill-based competitions with alumni as judges. Potentially create a homestay program to complement the Job Shadow Program. Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and Success Factors Exercise excellent judgment and sensitivity in the handling of confidential information. Is adept and diplomatic in dealing with both internal and external constituents. Possess strong organizational skills. Is flexible, self-motivated and has a strong sense of initiative. Pay strict attention to detail and accuracy. Effective in supervising other employees and understanding the shifting needs of the work day during the course of the year. Working Conditions Work is generally performed in an office environment. Ability to lift boxes or items up to 30 pounds or less is needed. Hybrid schedule (remote/in-office) is possible but not guaranteed. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree required, Master’s degree preferred. 5 to 10 years of relevant experience. Strong skills in oral and written communication. Experience with Microsoft Office and Google Suite. Kenyon College is a nationally prominent, private liberal arts college where academic excellence goes hand in hand with a strong sense of community and close relationships among students and professors. Compensation and Benefits Salaries at Kenyon are competitive and commensurate with experience. In addition to an attractive salary, Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook. Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d43b3c88 Last Name (required) 5bb19b89 Email (required) 0300bd6e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Office of the President Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Strategic Initiatives Project Coordinator in the Office of the President to support several of the college’s strategic initiatives, including Kenyon Keys, pre-college and destination programs, as well as academic and institutional partnerships, among others. Many of these programs are interdisciplinary and will cross traditional departmental boundaries, but they operate under the ultimate direction of the special assistant to the president for strategic initiatives and partnerships. The project coordinator will be an important partner for these programs, providing high-level logistical and administrative support, as well as occasional general support for the president’s division. This is a twelve-month position that will support logistics, maintain records, handle financial transactions, and support meetings and events. Notably, this position may serve as the on-site liaison for one or more of the Kenyon destination city programs, so some episodic summer travel may be required. This is a new position connected to the college's strategic initiatives; therefore, it will evolve over time as programs develop and change, and the project coordinator will have the opportunity to participate in that evolution. Assistant Director of Student Engagement (11 month) Ohio Five Colleges, Ohio Student Engagement Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Assistant Director of Student Engagement. In cooperation with other Student Affairs staff members, the Assistant Director shares an awareness of and concern for all aspects of student academic, residential, and co-curricular life. In particular, the Assistant Director of Student Engagement will support the ongoing work of student organization finance management and will serve as the department’s advisor to the campus programming board. The Assistant Director of Student Engagement is an eleven (11) month reporting position.  The work of the Assistant Director of Student Engagement includes regular evening and weekend responsibilities. Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Address Gambier, Ohio 43022, USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Youtube Cookie Preferences Policies © 2026 Kenyon College Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With th