    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/office-coordinator-for-the-office-of-residential-life-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator for the Office of Residential Life",
      "description": "Office Coordinator for the Office of Residential Life - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Back to Kenyon College Website My Profile Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Office Coordinator for the Office of Residential Life 493362 Gambier, OH, Ohio Housing and Residential Life Non-Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Office Coordinator for the Office of Residential Life.  The Office Coordinator is a member of the Office of Residential Life, reporting directly to the Director of Residential Life and supports the mission of the College by overseeing the day-to-day management of the Residential Life office suite. This is a part-time, with benefits position, working approximately 35 hours per week for 11 months (approximately 1668 hours annually). The hourly rate of pay for this non-exempt position is $17.96. The Office of Residential Life provides leadership, goals, and program implementation for Kenyon’s residential communities, housing operations, facility and occupancy management, and new student programs. Professional staff members and student leaders work together to cultivate safe and inclusive living communities. Kenyon’s fully-residential housing program includes 30 different residential spaces from traditional residence halls to apartments and suites. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS Serve as a member of the Residential Life team responsible for providing leadership, goals, and program implementation for approximately 1600 undergraduate students. Hire, train, supervise and evaluate 4-6 undergraduate Front Desk Workers. Maintain Residential Life digital presence via website, email, social media, written publications, posters, bulletin boards, and KCon. Coordinate new staff onboarding and training (office, computer, and phone line set-up, business cards, name tags, etc.). Keep office suite organized, manage supply inventory, and submit maintenance requests. Assist in coordinating the break housing process. Effectively coordinate and communicate with residents to ensure their needs are met and their experiences are positive by managing the Office of Residential Life correspondence through email, phone, and in-person interactions. Co-coordinate follow-up responses to housing selection questions and needs. Assist with the coordination and effective implementation of administrative processes, including but not limited to, residence hall openings/closings, room inspections and the housing selection process. Planning staff recognition and staff development events for the Office of Residential Life. Assist with the management of auxiliary spaces, both current and future. Conduct other duties as assigned by the Director of Residential Life. WORKING CONDITIONS Regular business hours are traditionally 8:30am - 4:30pm. Work is generally performed in an office environment; however, supervision of student leaders and oversight of residential areas requires the ability to navigate between residential facilities, moving through long hallways, being in buildings without air conditioning, and being outside in various weather conditions. Must also be able to lift boxes of items up to 30 pounds, move tables, chairs, and other furniture. Requires a valid driver’s license and ability to meet campus requirements to drive campus vehicles, in order to transport students and other items on occasion. Must be able to work evenings and weekends, including times when the College is closed; this includes the ability to travel and work during inclement weather or other exceptional conditions. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS The Office Coordinator will have 2-3 years of professional office experience, preferably in a higher education setting. Candidates must have an appreciation for the value of a residential, liberal arts education and should possess energy and enthusiasm for working with undergraduate students.  The successful candidate will also possess strong skills in organizational management, task completion, and have excellent written and oral communication skills.  Proficiency with the Microsoft Office suite, Google products, Campus Reports, and Banner data management system is highly desirable.  Ability to lift and carry 20 pounds, unassisted. Benefits Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) c19cfd60 Last Name (required) edf3044b Email (required) fc679128 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Strategic Initiative Project Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Office of the President Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Strategic Initiatives Project Coordinator in the Office of the President to support several of the college’s strategic initiatives, including Kenyon Keys, pre-college and destination programs, as well as academic and institutional partnerships, among others. Many of these programs are interdisciplinary and will cross traditional departmental boundaries, but they operate under the ultimate direction of the special assistant to the president for strategic initiatives and partnerships. The project coordinator will be an important partner for these programs, providing high-level logistical and administrative support, as well as occasional general support for the president’s division. This is a twelve-month position that will support logistics, maintain records, handle financial transactions, and support meetings and events. Notably, this position may serve as the on-site liaison for one or more of the Kenyon destination city programs, so some episodic summer travel may be required. This is a new position connected to the college's strategic initiatives; therefore, it will evolve over time as programs develop and change, and the project coordinator will have the opportunity to participate in that evolution. Student Accounts Coordinator Gambier, OH, Ohio Accounting Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to serve in the position of Student Accounts Coordinator for the Accounting Office. The hourly rate of pay for this full-time with benefits position is $17.96. Successful completion of duties requires a thorough understanding of, and adherence to, College Policies. Willingness and ability to work collaboratively as well as independently is required. General responsibility includes assistance in the management and maintenance of student account records, billings, receipts, maintenance of department records on Federal Perkins and Institutional student loans. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 8d09bc10 Last Name (required) d4fda514 Email (required) d6b8d329 Job Alert 582302c6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Housing and Residential Life Housing and Residential Life Employment Type Non-Exempt Staff Non-Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Address Gambier, Ohio 43022, USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Youtube Cookie Preferences Policies © 2026 Kenyon College Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
