    "https://careers.kenyon.edu/jobs/student-accounts-coordinator-gambier-oh-ohio-united-states-ab2b8926-9706-4700-b293-bf5e176c60d2": {
      "title": "Student Accounts Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Accounts Coordinator - Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Back to Kenyon College Website My Profile Kiosk mode Job Opportunities Student Accounts Coordinator 493351 Gambier, OH, Ohio Accounting Non-Exempt Staff Add to favorites View favorites Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to serve in the position of Student Accounts Coordinator for the Accounting Office. The hourly rate of pay for this full-time, with benefits, position is $17.96. Successful completion of duties requires a thorough understanding of, and adherence to, College Policies. Willingness and ability to work collaboratively as well as independently is required. General responsibility includes assistance in the management and maintenance of student account records, billings, receipts, maintenance of department records on Federal Perkins and Institutional student loans. Duties of this position include, but are not limited to the following: Communication with students, parents, student loan borrowers and responsible parties. Posting of miscellaneous charges, student payments, and receipts. Reconciliation of general ledger accounts and running the monthly billing process. Maintaining student loan records and processing payments. The candidate must be punctual, reliable and possess the ability to work with interruptions during periods of peak activity. Effective and professional communication skills are critical, as well as a high degree of organization and time management. Skilled use of Microsoft Word and Excel is required. Experience in an accounting or finance office and an Associate degree in accounting is preferred. Benefits Kenyon offers benefits for employees and their family members. Children of employees are eligible for 100% tuition waivers at Kenyon, and through the Great Lakes Colleges Association , children of employees are eligible for 90% tuition waivers at twenty-three other of the nation's finest liberal arts colleges. We also offer health, dental and vision insurance, TIAA retirement, and many other benefits , including provisions for a spouse, families, and domestic partners. Details about benefits as well as conditions of employment are described more fully in our Staff Handbook . Kenyon is a unique place to live and work. To discover why it should be your next home, click here . Kenyon College is an equal opportunity employer, and we welcome applications from all qualified individuals. It is the College's policy to evaluate qualified applicants without regard to race, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, gender, gender identity, gender expression, sexual orientation, physical and/or mental disability, age, religion, medical condition, veteran status, marital status, or any other characteristic protected by institutional policy or state, local, or federal law. Kenyon College has a strong commitment to an inclusive environment that welcomes all voices and perspectives. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) e488ea4e Last Name (required) 2580ea63 Email (required) 5249742f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Executive Assistant for The Kenyon Review Gambier, OH, Ohio Kenyon Review The Executive Assistant plays a central role in supporting the organization's leadership and ensuring smooth day-to-day operations by providing including grant coordination, gift acknowledgement, board administration, and conference/event logistics. The ideal candidate is highly organized, proactive, and passionate about supporting the literary arts. Office Coordinator for the Office of Residential Life Gambier, OH, Ohio Housing and Residential Life The Residential Life Office Coordinator is a member of the Office of Residential Life, reporting directly to the Director of Residential Life. The Residential Life Office Coordinator supports the mission of the College by overseeing the day-to-day management of the Residential Life office suite. Telecommunications Officer, Part-Time Gambier, OH, Ohio Office of Campus Safety Kenyon College is conducting a search for a qualified candidate to fill the position of Campus Safety Telecommunications Officer, Part-Time. Hours worked per week and shifts worked will be dependent on coverage needs, including weekends and possibly holidays. The rate of pay is $18.50 per hour between the hours of 7:00am to 3:00pm, $20.00 between the hours of 3:00pm to 7:00am. Part-Time Campus Safety Telecommunication Officers receive double their hourly pay rate when scheduled to work a shift during recognized college holidays. This is a collectively bargained position and without benefits. Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) 0e131db7 Last Name (required) e73a2ff8 Email (required) 18edb52f Job Alert 8c22630a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Accounting Accounting Employment Type Non-Exempt Staff Non-Exempt Staff Locations Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Gambier, OH, Ohio, United States Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Address Gambier, Ohio 43022, USA Phone 740-427-5000 Connect Facebook LinkedIn Instagram Youtube Cookie Preferences Policies © 2026 Kenyon College Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
